{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1378662-newbie-qs-about-actions","id":1378662,"title":"newbie Qs about actions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-04T19:56:50-07:00","id":1378662,"title":"newbie Qs about actions","content":"Hey, all. Been lurking for a while, first post. Be nice. \ud83d\ude0a I bought a few nWoD (1e) books several years ago and still have some PDFs, but never got a chance to play. Recently, I picked up the CofD core book (the PDF about a week ago, the core book in the mail today), and I have a couple of players who are interested, so I\u2019m doing my best to learn the rules. I was hoping I could run a few things by you experts so you could point out any mistakes.<br /> <br /> Okay, as far as actions go, there are three main types:<ul><li>Instant: takes a few seconds, uses character\u2019s turn</li> <li>Reflexive: takes no time, doesn't use character\u2019s turn</li> <li>Extended: takes several actions, each taking some GM-determined time, requires a total number of successes</li> </ul>Then there\u2019s Contested Actions, which are an instant action vs. a reflexive action:<ul><li>Initiator's roll: instant action, attribute + skill</li> <li>Target's roll: reflexive action, attribute + skill or attribute (needn\u2019t be a resistance attribute)</li> <li>Whoever rolls more successes wins</li> <li>Loser\u2019s successes are not subtracted from the winner\u2019s successes for the purposes of determining whether an exceptional success was achieved</li> <li>Used when the result is all or nothing, and the number of successes is irrelevant (except for determining whether it was an exceptional success)</li> </ul>Resistances<ul><li>Attacker rolls attribute + skill - defender's resistance attribute or defense (as relevant)</li> <li>The attacker's number of successes are applied per the action (e.g., damage to health)</li> <li>Used when the exact number of successes is relevant (e.g., combat)</li> </ul>Okay so far? Now, I\u2019ve seen (from lurking and searching) that there\u2019s some confusion and/or difference of opinion about the contested actions vs. resistances, and I was a bit confused about that myself, until I realized that the only thing that was confusing me were some of the examples on pages 70-71, which I think are simply wrong, and weren\u2019t caught in proofing. Sticking with a strict reading of the rules-as-written, Fast-Talk and Interrogation should be contested actions, since the number of successes is irrelevant; this seems confirmed by nWoD 1e core, p.38. If that\u2019s right, then Argument and Intimidation should be contested actions as well. Fortunately, the section starts with &quot;Here are some sample [not &quot;definitive&quot;] ways you can [not &quot;must&quot;] apply your Skills. Remember you can invent your own at any time [including using them as contest actions].&quot; So if I take the spirit of that sentence to heart, and don\u2019t worry about the screwy examples, everything seems to fall into place. However, I wanted to make sure that I wasn\u2019t missing anything. <br /> <br /> For example, all of those screwy examples seem to be social conflicts. Is there anything about social conflicts that makes the number of the attacker\u2019s successes relevant, and thus requires using resistances instead of contested actions? I\u2019ve been looking at the social maneuvering rules, but I haven\u2019t seen anything so far.<br /> <br /> Also, what else besides combat actually requires resistances? What other sorts of actions have results where the number of successes matter against a defender of some kind? Does that come up at all in the core book, or is that just something that happens in the other CofD books (e.g., various supernatural attacks and such)?<br /> Thanks much for reading, and thanks very much in advance for any help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26064-theophiluscarter","name":"TheophilusCarter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26064_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T00:44:00-07:00","id":1378692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheophilusCarter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1378662-newbie-qs-about-actions#post1378662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then there\u2019s Contested Actions, which are an instant action vs. a reflexive action:</div> </div> </div> </div>Contested actions don't have to be reflexive for the &quot;defender&quot; as it were. The action types for contested actions are determined the same way as normal. Contested actions are frequently instant vs. reflexive to avoid &quot;action lock&quot; where you can force someone to lose an action by engaging them in a contested roll off, or have multiple people using the same contested action on someone so they can only roll off against one of them.<br /> <br /> You should use your best judgement on this.<br /> <br /> Also, contested or resisted actions do not have to be Attribute + Skill, even if that's going to be the most common for normal humans. Attribute + Attribute rolls, or supernatural power rolls with their own traits, are possible. Basically don't get too locked into a specific mindset here.<br /> <br /> In general, you can also mix and match things. You can have extended contested actions, or contested resisted actions, or anything else that makes sense. Contested and Resisted are not opposites, but the rules want to provide a solid idea of when to apply each.<br /> <br /> For example, you could settled a arm wrestling contest with Strength + Athletics - Stamina for both sides. It's contested because the results are binary, but also resisted because the number of successes does matter; and more importantly it lets you have some variety in ways to be good at it which is more fun than being to strict with the guidelines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Loser\u2019s successes are not subtracted from the winner\u2019s successes for the purposes of determining whether an exceptional success was achieved </div> </div> </div>Unless specifically stated, the loser's successes are not subtracted from the winners period. While there is no strict mechanical difference between winning a roll off with 1 success vs 0. or 4 successes vs. 1 success, it should inform how you describe the results. If you're rolling an extended contented contested action (such as characters trying to climb up a rock wall to see who gets their first) both sides add up their successes towards the total.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if I take the spirit of that sentence to heart, and don\u2019t worry about the screwy examples, everything seems to fall into place. </div> </div> </div>In general, this is a very good mental note towards interpreting Onyx Path writing. People have their opinions about it, but the writers intend for spirit to matter more than examples for these things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what else besides combat actually requires resistances? </div> </div> </div>I think you're getting a bit hung up on the guidelines. Remember the book uses &quot;number of successes matters vs. not,&quot; if you're not sure which to apply; not as a hard rule.<br /> <br /> Nothing requires resistance (combat handled with Down and Dirty doesn't use it). Nothing requires contested.<br /> <br /> That said, you'll see a lot of examples of resisted actions that ignore the guidelines because, among certain issues, there isn't a dice-pool for the defender. In Forcing Doors, Doors act as the targets resistance, even though the number of successes doesn't matter, because there's no Doors dice-pool.<br /> <br /> There's also more resisted rolls in supernatural powers since they're more likely to have scaled effects.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T04:53:26-07:00","id":1378725,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the response, lots of good info to think about!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26064-theophiluscarter","name":"TheophilusCarter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26064_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T14:59:30-07:00","id":1378852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheophilusCarter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1378662-newbie-qs-about-actions#post1378662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, all. Been lurking for a while, first post. Be nice. \ud83d\ude0a I bought a few nWoD (1e) books several years ago and still have some PDFs, but never got a chance to play. Recently, I picked up the CofD core book (the PDF about a week ago, the core book in the mail today), and I have a couple of players who are interested, so I\u2019m doing my best to learn the rules. I was hoping I could run a few things by you experts so you could point out any mistakes.....<br /> <br /> [Many good questions, deleted]</div> </div> </div> </div>How do these rolls change when facing a Spirit/Angel/Ghost - beings that only have Power, Finesse and Resistance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T17:14:04-07:00","id":1378884,"title":"","content":"The Ephemeral Entities section details how to determine what they roll instead of normal dice-pools. Generally it will be: Attribute (general tasks), Attribute + Rank (tasks related to their nature), and Attribute + Attribute (specified tasks).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T17:56:06-07:00","id":1378889,"title":"","content":"More good Q&amp;A, thanks!<br /> <br /> BTW, I'm also finding it really helpful to look some of this up in the nWoD core rules. They often explained things more fully there. I suspect they needed to be more concise for CofD, so they could include so much more good stuff in the core book, but what they gained in conciseness they may have lost in clarity ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26064-theophiluscarter","name":"TheophilusCarter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26064_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T18:44:56-07:00","id":1378898,"title":"","content":"That's certainly a fair criticism of some of the CofD/2e stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}